 *       B[i][j] = (i*(j+2) % nj) / nj;
 *
 * Note: In C, arrays are laid out as C[NI][NJ] and accessed as C[i][j].
 * In Halide, the first dimension is the fastest varying, so we store C in a
 * Halide::Buffer of shape (NJ, NI) and access as C(j, i).
